  "problem": {
    "id": "train-3225",
    "question": "Chris bought 8 movies on DVD for $12 each and 4 movies on Blu-ray for $18 each. What is the average price he paid per movie?",
    "gold": "14",
    "answer": "He spent a total of 8 * $12 + 4 * $18 = $<<8*12+4*18=168>>168\nHe bought a total of 8 + 4 = <<8+4=12>>12 movies.\nThe average price is $168 / 12 = $<<168/12=14>>14 per movie.\n#### 14"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average price Chris paid per movie, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the DVDs.\n2. Calculate the total cost of the Blu-rays.\n3. Find the total number of movies.\n4. Calculate the total cost of all the movies.\n5. Divide the total cost by the total number of movies to find the average price per movie.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the DVDs:\n   Chris bought 8 DVDs at $12 each.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost of DVDs} = 8 \\times 12 = 96\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the total cost of the Blu-rays:\n   Chris bought 4 Blu-rays at $18 each.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost of Blu-rays} = 4 \\times 18 = 72\n   \\]\n\n3. Find the total number of movies:\n   Chris bought 8 DVDs and 4 Blu-rays.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of movies} = 8 + 4 = 12\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate the total cost of all the movies:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost of all movies} = 96 + 72 = 168\n   \\]\n\n5. Divide the total cost by the total number of movies to find the average price per movie:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average price per movie} = \\frac{168}{12} = 14\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the average price Chris paid per movie is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
